              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>The patient shows a significantly elevated PSA level (14.6 ng/mL; normal 0–4 ng/mL), which is unexpected in a 62-year-old female, as PSA is typically associated with prostate tissue. This result may indicate a preanalytical or clerical error, or rare ectopic PSA production. Recommend verification of patient identity, sample labeling, and clinical correlation.</td></tr></table></div>"
